{
  "duration": 67.639,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 0.299,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.759,
      "end": 1.679,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.24,
      "end": 3.959,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.42,
      "end": 5.859,
      "text": "Now in this problem, we are given that"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.44,
      "end": 7.719,
      "text": "tan of theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.22,
      "end": 10.239,
      "text": "is equal to five divided by 12,"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.719,
      "end": 12.519,
      "text": "and theta is an acute angle."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.0,
      "end": 16.379,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the value of sine theta."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.279,
      "end": 18.059,
      "text": "Tan of theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.379,
      "end": 18.699,
      "text": "means"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.159,
      "end": 21.799,
      "text": "opposite side divided by adjacent side."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.279,
      "end": 26.379,
      "text": "So we can say opposite side divided by adjacent side is equal to five"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.799,
      "end": 27.799,
      "text": "divided by 12."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.299,
      "end": 34.139,
      "text": "This means we can take the opposite side as five units and the adjacent side as 12 units."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.739,
      "end": 35.939,
      "text": "Since we know these two sides,"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.38,
      "end": 40.0,
      "text": "we can find the hypotenuse using the Pythagoras theorem."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.34,
      "end": 42.5,
      "text": "The hypotenuse is equal to the square root of"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.059,
      "end": 44.679,
      "text": "five square plus 12 square."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.259,
      "end": 46.34,
      "text": "After simplifying this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.739,
      "end": 49.079,
      "text": "the hypotenuse is equal to 13."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.5,
      "end": 52.919,
      "text": "We needed this value because sine theta means"
    },
    {
      "start": 53.579,
      "end": 56.159,
      "text": "opposite side divided by hypotenuse."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.639,
      "end": 60.299,
      "text": "So sine theta is equal to five divided by 13."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.139,
      "end": 67.639,
      "text": "Hence, the value of sine theta is five by 13, so the correct option is option C."
    }
  ],
